    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="shopify-policy__body">
    <div class="rte">
<p><em>Last updated: 29 October 2026</em></p>

<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<p>Nailogy ("we", "us", "our") runs the online shop at nailogy.co.uk, selling professional nail supplies to customers in the United Kingdom. We are the data controller for the personal information described in this policy.</p>
<p>Contact: <a href="mailto:info@nailogy.co.uk">info@nailogy.co.uk</a></p>
<p>This policy explains what personal information we collect, why we use it, who we share it with and the rights you have under the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR), the Data Protection Act 2018 and the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR).</p>

<h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Contact and delivery details:</strong> your name, email address, phone number, billing and delivery address.</li>
<li><strong>Order information:</strong> the products you buy, order history, returns and refunds.</li>
<li><strong>Payment information:</strong> payments are processed securely by our payment providers. We do not see or store your full card number.</li>
<li><strong>Account information:</strong> if you create an account, your login details and saved preferences.</li>
<li><strong>Communications:</strong> messages you send us by email or through our contact form.</li>
<li><strong>Device and usage information:</strong> your IP address, browser and device type, and how you use our website, collected through cookies and similar technologies (see section 8).</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How we use your information and our lawful bases</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>To process and deliver your orders</strong>, take payment, handle returns and provide customer service. <em>Lawful basis: performance of a contract.</em></li>
<li><strong>To meet our legal obligations</strong>, such as keeping tax and accounting records and responding to lawful requests. <em>Lawful basis: legal obligation.</em></li>
<li><strong>To keep our shop secure</strong> and prevent fraud, and to improve our website and products. <em>Lawful basis: legitimate interests.</em></li>
<li><strong>To send you marketing emails</strong> about our products and offers. <em>Lawful basis: your consent, or for existing customers, the "soft opt-in" under PECR.</em> You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in every email.</li>
<li><strong>To use non-essential cookies</strong> for analytics and advertising. <em>Lawful basis: your consent.</em></li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Who we share your information with</h2>
<p>We only share your information where necessary, with:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Shopify</strong>, which hosts our online shop and processes orders on our behalf.</li>
<li><strong>Payment providers</strong>, to process your payment securely.</li>
<li><strong>Delivery companies</strong> such as Royal Mail, to deliver your order.</li>
<li><strong>Email and analytics providers</strong>, to send our emails and understand how our website is used.</li>
<li><strong>Advertising partners</strong> such as Google and Meta, only if you consent to marketing cookies.</li>
<li><strong>Professional advisers and authorities</strong>, where required by law.</li>
</ul>
<p>We never sell your personal information.</p>

<h2>5. International transfers</h2>
<p>Some of our service providers, including Shopify, may process your information outside the UK. Where this happens, we make sure appropriate safeguards are in place, such as UK adequacy regulations or the International Data Transfer Agreement / Addendum approved by the ICO.</p>

<h2>6. How long we keep your information</h2>
<ul>
<li>Order and transaction records: 6 years after the end of the financial year, as required for UK tax purposes.</li>
<li>Customer accounts: until you ask us to close your account.</li>
<li>Marketing preferences: until you unsubscribe.</li>
<li>Customer service messages: up to 2 years after our last contact.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Keeping your information secure</h2>
<p>We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal information. Our website uses secure (HTTPS) connections, and payments are handled by PCI-compliant providers. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, but we work to protect your information.</p>

<h2>8. Cookies</h2>
<p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. We use:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies:</strong> needed for the shop to work, for example to keep items in your basket and to complete checkout. These don't need your consent.</li>
<li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> help us understand how visitors use our website so we can improve it.</li>
<li><strong>Marketing cookies:</strong> used by us and our advertising partners to show you relevant adverts.</li>
</ul>
<p>We only use analytics and marketing cookies if you accept them in our cookie banner. You can change your choice at any time using the cookie settings link on our website, or by clearing cookies in your browser settings.</p>

<h2>9. Your rights</h2>
<p>Under UK data protection law, you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
<li>access the personal information we hold about you;</li>
<li>ask us to correct inaccurate information;</li>
<li>ask us to delete your information;</li>
<li>object to or ask us to restrict how we use your information;</li>
<li>ask for your information to be transferred to another organisation (data portability);</li>
<li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on consent;</li>
<li>object to direct marketing at any time.</li>
</ul>
<p>To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:info@nailogy.co.uk">info@nailogy.co.uk</a>. We will respond within one month. We may need to confirm your identity first.</p>

<h2>10. Complaints</h2>
<p>If you have a concern about how we use your personal information, please contact us first so we can try to put it right.</p>
<p>You also have the right to complain to the UK's data protection regulator, the <strong>Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Website: <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a></li>
<li>Helpline: 0303 123 1113</li>
</ul>

<h2>11. Children</h2>
<p>Our shop is not intended for children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect information about them.</p>

<h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page, with the date it was last updated.</p>

<h2>13. Contact us</h2>
<p>Nailogy<br>Email: <a href="mailto:info@nailogy.co.uk">info@nailogy.co.uk</a><br>Website: www.nailogy.co.uk</p>
